    "title": "Mary Gay Scanlon criticizes presidential actions and DOJ delays in recent posts - South Delco News",
    "text": "Congresswoman Mary Gay Scanlon, who represents Pennsylvania’s 5th district in the U.S. Congress, posted a series of critical tweets on December 12, 2025, addressing topics ranging from White House policies to the release of government files.\nIn one post at 19:16 UTC, Scanlon questioned statements made by the President regarding school supplies and economic conditions: “Wonder if the President saw this before he told Americans their kids only need 1 or 2 pencils? Or when he told Americans that prices are going down?”\nShortly after, at 19:29 UTC, she commented on historical preservation at the White House: “The White House is the people’s house. No President should be allowed to erase the building’s history without going through the proper processes.”\nLater that evening at 20:52 UTC, Scanlon addressed delays in releasing files related to Jeffrey Epstein by the Department of Justice (DOJ): “Abhorrent. Shocking that the DOJ hasn’t released the Epstein files yet. The survivors deserve justice.”\nScanlon has served as a member of Congress since replacing Pat Meehan in 2018 and continues to represent Pennsylvania’s 5th District. Born in Watertown, New York in 1959 and currently residing in Swarthmore, she holds degrees from Colgate University and the University of Pennsylvania.",
